{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function injectAsyncDebouncer<TFn, TSelected>(\n   fn,\n   options,\nselector?): AngularAsyncDebouncer<TFn, TSelected>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/angular-pacer/src/async-debouncer/injectAsyncDebouncer.ts#L126","children":[{"type":"text","value":"async-debouncer/injectAsyncDebouncer.ts:126"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An Angular function that creates and manages an AsyncDebouncer instance."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is a lower-level function that provides direct access to the AsyncDebouncer's functionality.\nThis allows you to integrate it with any state management solution you prefer."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function provides async debouncing functionality with promise support, error handling,\nretry capabilities, and abort support."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The debouncer will only execute the function after the specified wait time has elapsed\nsince the last call. If the function is called again before the wait time expires, the\ntimer resets and starts waiting again."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"state-management-and-selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State Management and Selector"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The function uses TanStack Store for state management and wraps it with Angular signals.\nThe "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"selector"},{"type":"text","value":" parameter allows you to specify which state changes will trigger signal updates,\noptimizing performance by preventing unnecessary updates when irrelevant state changes occur."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function. This prevents unnecessary updates and gives you\nfull control over when your component tracks state changes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Available state properties:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"canLeadingExecute"},{"type":"text","value":": Whether the debouncer can execute on the leading edge"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"errorCount"},{"type":"text","value":": Number of function executions that have resulted in errors"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isExecuting"},{"type":"text","value":": Whether the debounced function is currently executing asynchronously"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isPending"},{"type":"text","value":": Whether the debouncer is waiting for the timeout to trigger execution"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lastArgs"},{"type":"text","value":": The arguments from the most recent call to maybeExecute"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lastResult"},{"type":"text","value":": The result from the most recent successful function execution"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"settleCount"},{"type":"text","value":": Number of function executions that have completed (either successfully or with errors)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":": Current execution status ('disabled' | 'idle' | 'pending' | 'executing' | 'settled')"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"successCount"},{"type":"text","value":": Number of function executions that have completed successfully"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"cleanup-on-destroy","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cleanup on Destroy"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, the function cancels any pending execution and aborts in-flight work when the component is destroyed.\nUse the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onUnmount"},{"type":"text","value":" option to customize this. For example, to flush pending work instead:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const debouncer = injectAsyncDebouncer(fn, {\n  wait: 500,\n  onUnmount: (d) => d.flush()\n});","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When using onUnmount with flush, guard your callbacks since the component may already be destroyed."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tfn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AnyAsyncFunction"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tselected","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":" = {\n}"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/AngularPacerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AngularPacerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/AngularAsyncDebouncerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AngularAsyncDebouncerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">>"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"selector?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/AngularAsyncDebouncer.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AngularAsyncDebouncer"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TFn"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst debouncer = injectAsyncDebouncer(\n  async (query: string) => {\n    const response = await fetch(`/api/search?q=${query}`);\n    return response.json();\n  },\n  { wait: 500 }\n);\n\n// Opt-in to track isExecuting changes (optimized for loading states)\nconst debouncer = injectAsyncDebouncer(\n  async (query: string) => fetchSearchResults(query),\n  { wait: 500 },\n  (state) => ({ isExecuting: state.isExecuting, isPending: state.isPending })\n);\n\n// In an event handler\nconst handleChange = async (e: Event) => {\n  const target = e.target as HTMLInputElement;\n  const result = await debouncer.maybeExecute(target.value);\n  console.log('Search results:', result);\n};\n\n// Access the selected state\nconst { isExecuting, errorCount } = debouncer.state();","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"state-management-and-selector","text":"State Management and Selector","level":2},{"id":"cleanup-on-destroy","text":"Cleanup on Destroy","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tfn","text":"TFn","level":3},{"id":"tselected","text":"TSelected","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"fn","text":"fn","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"selector","text":"selector?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction injectAsyncDebouncer<TFn, TSelected>(\n   fn,\n   options,\nselector?): AngularAsyncDebouncer<TFn, TSelected>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [async-debouncer/injectAsyncDebouncer.ts:126](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/angular-pacer/src/async-debouncer/injectAsyncDebouncer.ts#L126)\n\nAn Angular function that creates and manages an AsyncDebouncer instance.\n\nThis is a lower-level function that provides direct access to the AsyncDebouncer's functionality.\nThis allows you to integrate it with any state management solution you prefer.\n\nThis function provides async debouncing functionality with promise support, error handling,\nretry capabilities, and abort support.\n\nThe debouncer will only execute the function after the specified wait time has elapsed\nsince the last call. If the function is called again before the wait time expires, the\ntimer resets and starts waiting again.\n\n## State Management and Selector\n\nThe function uses TanStack Store for state management and wraps it with Angular signals.\nThe `selector` parameter allows you to specify which state changes will trigger signal updates,\noptimizing performance by preventing unnecessary updates when irrelevant state changes occur.\n\n**By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions** and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function. This prevents unnecessary updates and gives you\nfull control over when your component tracks state changes.\n\nAvailable state properties:\n- `canLeadingExecute`: Whether the debouncer can execute on the leading edge\n- `errorCount`: Number of function executions that have resulted in errors\n- `isExecuting`: Whether the debounced function is currently executing asynchronously\n- `isPending`: Whether the debouncer is waiting for the timeout to trigger execution\n- `lastArgs`: The arguments from the most recent call to maybeExecute\n- `lastResult`: The result from the most recent successful function execution\n- `settleCount`: Number of function executions that have completed (either successfully or with errors)\n- `status`: Current execution status ('disabled' | 'idle' | 'pending' | 'executing' | 'settled')\n- `successCount`: Number of function executions that have completed successfully\n\n## Cleanup on Destroy\n\nBy default, the function cancels any pending execution and aborts in-flight work when the component is destroyed.\nUse the `onUnmount` option to customize this. For example, to flush pending work instead:\n\n```ts\nconst debouncer = injectAsyncDebouncer(fn, {\n  wait: 500,\n  onUnmount: (d) => d.flush()\n});\n```\n\nWhen using onUnmount with flush, guard your callbacks since the component may already be destroyed.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* `AnyAsyncFunction`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\n### options\n\n[`AngularPacerOptions`](../type-aliases/AngularPacerOptions.md)\\<[`AngularAsyncDebouncerOptions`](../interfaces/AngularAsyncDebouncerOptions.md)\\<`TFn`, `TSelected`\\>\\>\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n[`AngularAsyncDebouncer`](../interfaces/AngularAsyncDebouncer.md)\\<`TFn`, `TSelected`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\n// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst debouncer = injectAsyncDebouncer(\n  async (query: string) => {\n    const response = await fetch(`/api/search?q=${query}`);\n    return response.json();\n  },\n  { wait: 500 }\n);\n\n// Opt-in to track isExecuting changes (optimized for loading states)\nconst debouncer = injectAsyncDebouncer(\n  async (query: string) => fetchSearchResults(query),\n  { wait: 500 },\n  (state) => ({ isExecuting: state.isExecuting, isPending: state.isPending })\n);\n\n// In an event handler\nconst handleChange = async (e: Event) => {\n  const target = e.target as HTMLInputElement;\n  const result = await debouncer.maybeExecute(target.value);\n  console.log('Search results:', result);\n};\n\n// Access the selected state\nconst { isExecuting, errorCount } = debouncer.state();\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: injectAsyncDebouncer\ntitle: injectAsyncDebouncer\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction injectAsyncDebouncer<TFn, TSelected>(\n   fn,\n   options,\nselector?): AngularAsyncDebouncer<TFn, TSelected>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [async-debouncer/injectAsyncDebouncer.ts:126](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/angular-pacer/src/async-debouncer/injectAsyncDebouncer.ts#L126)\n\nAn Angular function that creates and manages an AsyncDebouncer instance.\n\nThis is a lower-level function that provides direct access to the AsyncDebouncer's functionality.\nThis allows you to integrate it with any state management solution you prefer.\n\nThis function provides async debouncing functionality with promise support, error handling,\nretry capabilities, and abort support.\n\nThe debouncer will only execute the function after the specified wait time has elapsed\nsince the last call. If the function is called again before the wait time expires, the\ntimer resets and starts waiting again.\n\n## State Management and Selector\n\nThe function uses TanStack Store for state management and wraps it with Angular signals.\nThe `selector` parameter allows you to specify which state changes will trigger signal updates,\noptimizing performance by preventing unnecessary updates when irrelevant state changes occur.\n\n**By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions** and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function. This prevents unnecessary updates and gives you\nfull control over when your component tracks state changes.\n\nAvailable state properties:\n- `canLeadingExecute`: Whether the debouncer can execute on the leading edge\n- `errorCount`: Number of function executions that have resulted in errors\n- `isExecuting`: Whether the debounced function is currently executing asynchronously\n- `isPending`: Whether the debouncer is waiting for the timeout to trigger execution\n- `lastArgs`: The arguments from the most recent call to maybeExecute\n- `lastResult`: The result from the most recent successful function execution\n- `settleCount`: Number of function executions that have completed (either successfully or with errors)\n- `status`: Current execution status ('disabled' | 'idle' | 'pending' | 'executing' | 'settled')\n- `successCount`: Number of function executions that have completed successfully\n\n## Cleanup on Destroy\n\nBy default, the function cancels any pending execution and aborts in-flight work when the component is destroyed.\nUse the `onUnmount` option to customize this. For example, to flush pending work instead:\n\n```ts\nconst debouncer = injectAsyncDebouncer(fn, {\n  wait: 500,\n  onUnmount: (d) => d.flush()\n});\n```\n\nWhen using onUnmount with flush, guard your callbacks since the component may already be destroyed.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TFn\n\n`TFn` *extends* `AnyAsyncFunction`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n`TFn`\n\n### options\n\n[`AngularPacerOptions`](../type-aliases/AngularPacerOptions.md)\\<[`AngularAsyncDebouncerOptions`](../interfaces/AngularAsyncDebouncerOptions.md)\\<`TFn`, `TSelected`\\>\\>\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n[`AngularAsyncDebouncer`](../interfaces/AngularAsyncDebouncer.md)\\<`TFn`, `TSelected`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\n// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst debouncer = injectAsyncDebouncer(\n  async (query: string) => {\n    const response = await fetch(`/api/search?q=${query}`);\n    return response.json();\n  },\n  { wait: 500 }\n);\n\n// Opt-in to track isExecuting changes (optimized for loading states)\nconst debouncer = injectAsyncDebouncer(\n  async (query: string) => fetchSearchResults(query),\n  { wait: 500 },\n  (state) => ({ isExecuting: state.isExecuting, isPending: state.isPending })\n);\n\n// In an event handler\nconst handleChange = async (e: Event) => {\n  const target = e.target as HTMLInputElement;\n  const result = await debouncer.maybeExecute(target.value);\n  console.log('Search results:', result);\n};\n\n// Access the selected state\nconst { isExecuting, errorCount } = debouncer.state();\n```\n"}
